{"name":"Roaming Pony","hex":"#857373","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"roaming","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of roam"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An instance of wandering.","The ability to use a cell phone outside of its original registering zone."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roaming"},{"term":"pony","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small horse; specifically, any of several small breeds of horse under 14.2 hands at the withers.","A horse of any size."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To lead (a horse) from another horse.","To use a crib or cheat-sheet in translating."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pony"}],"entries":[{"title":"Roaming","blocks":[{"text":"Roaming is a Wireless telecommunication term that typically refers to a mobile phone or mobile device being used outside the range of its native network and connecting to another available cell network."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/T-Mobile_roaming_welcome_message_-_Redvers.jpg/330px-T-Mobile_roaming_welcome_message_-_Redvers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roaming","wikidata":"Q680016"},{"title":"Pony","blocks":[{"text":"A pony is a type of small horse, usually under a specific height at full maturity. Ponies often have thicker coats, manes and tails, compared to larger horses, and proportionally shorter legs, wider barrels, heavier bone, thicker necks and shorter heads. In modern use, breed registries and horse shows may define a pony as measuring at the withers below a certain height; height limits varying from about 14 hands to 14.3 hands. Some distinguish between horse or pony based on its breed or phenotype, regardless of its height. The word pony derives from the old French poulenet, a diminutive of poulain meaning foal, a young, immature horse. A full-sized horse may sometimes be called a pony as a term of endearment."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Gracie-rhs2005.jpg/330px-Gracie-rhs2005.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pony","wikidata":"Q188828"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Shetland_Pony_in_Harness_and_Cart.gif/500px-Shetland_Pony_in_Harness_and_Cart.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Shetland_Pony_in_Harness_and_Cart.gif/1280px-Shetland_Pony_in_Harness_and_Cart.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Shetland_Pony_in_Harness_and_Cart.gif/500px-Shetland_Pony_in_Harness_and_Cart.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Shetland pony shown in harness","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AShetland_Pony_in_Harness_and_Cart.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/SackOTatersPony.jpg/330px-SackOTatersPony.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/SackOTatersPony.jpg/330px-SackOTatersPony.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A pony foal","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASackOTatersPony.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Shetlands_in_Belgium.jpg/330px-Shetlands_in_Belgium.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Shetlands_in_Belgium.jpg/330px-Shetlands_in_Belgium.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Shetland pony is one of the smallest pony breed